<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4054"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 7:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very interesting post, Skov.  Thanks!  Would the <BR>massive bruising be caused by a beating, or from stangulation?  If from stangulation, would the <BR>bruising be strictly on the neck area?  Or all  <BR>over?  Possibly where all the ligatures wereplaced - legs, thighs, wrists? <BR>Quite frankly, I have a real tough time <BR>with psychics, only because they always claim <BR>to have foreknowledge in retrospect!  IOW, all <BR>the above claims could have easily been leaked <BR>out from the earlier investigations.  When did <BR>this psychic make these &#34;intuitive claims&#34;? I <BR>think we have all heard that the faucet was <BR>running, and that the angel doll was taken. I <BR>had not heard of the sodomy - in fact, that does <BR>somewhat surprise me. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
