<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4056"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 7:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, one thing that you are onto is the construction connection.  <BR> <BR>-BTK victim Nancy Fox worked for a constuction company as her full-time job and at Hertzberg&#39;s Jewlers as her second job. <BR>-BTK victim Shirley Vian&#39;s common-law husband Richard Vian worked for a construction company. <BR>-BTK victim Vicki Wegerle&#39;s husband Bill Wegerle worked as a self employed apartment maintainance man. <BR> <BR>A construction connection weaves it&#39;s way through the BTK case.  <BR>The question would be is there also a construction connection to the Otero&#39;s, Katheryn Bright and Anna Williams and does that common denominator lead to BTK?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
